+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The registry validates each model-supplied tool call against the JSON Schema registered for that tool before executing it.
+
+## Contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` that identifies missing required properties, wrong types, or enum violations by property path and constraint, without exposing input values in returned text or log lines; it does not call the executor for rejected input. Valid input reaches the executor unchanged, including extra properties, and an unknown tool name still throws `Unknown tool: <name>`. ([validated by: rejects required, type, and enum violations without exposing values or invoking the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L11)).
+- A static tool schema is compiled when `register` is called, and an uncompilable schema throws an error naming the tool at registration time. ([validated by: rejects an uncompilable static schema when the named tool is registered](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L47)).
+- A static tool uses its compiled schema across later executions. ([validated by: keeps a static schema compiled across ten executions](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L57)).
+- A function-valued tool definition resolves its schema for each call and validates against that call's schema. ([validated by: uses each function-valued definition schema at the call where it resolves](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L79)).
+- The orchestrator returns a schema rejection to the model as a tool result, so a corrected call can complete within the configured tool-round limit. ([validated by: returns a rejected tool call to the provider so a corrected retry completes](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L7)).
